h-academy-id "q-8231" :question/problem "If $z=3-4\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=3+4\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(3-4\\text{i})+(3+4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+3)+\\text{i}(-4+4) \\\\  & =6+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16423/selection/ea8c070ebcf07ae4fde114f8d5ccbf616648be25e4a1713c370eabfa2b0c2530" :answer/id #uuid "df9e7888-d2be-5bd0-8330-508007d20767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "85\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16423/selection/4ffc8a847b27b3b7ebbb549fb1cf5f4356d9f54bdbe679bff875c9355c41ace8" :answer/id #uuid "791c85f6-036e-5302-b391-62dada87e528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "97\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16423/selection/51b7e71ac415d62fcd6302db1c518c0badce55dda03eceebe662e87a5996a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "03a6240a-d4f7-531b-845f-02448db67f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16423/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "4684b083-df53-50af-b